  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821326">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">nonlinear parameter estimation (Dubinin–Astakhov model)</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">nonlinear estimation of Dubinin–Astakhov isotherm parameters</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This task performs nonlinear parameter estimation using equilibrium adsorption data to determine the theoretical Dubinin–Astakhov isotherm saturation capacitythe, Dubinin–Astakhov isotherm constant, and the Dubinin–Astakhov heterogeneity exponent. The nonlinear Dubinin–Astakhov equation is fitted directly to equilibrium adsorption values determined by experimental adsorption measurements, using the Polanyi potential to capture the effective adsorption work. Because the Dubinin–Astakhov model is temperature-dependent, it can consolidate multi-temperature data into a single characteristic curve that describes micropore filling behavior.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P1684 xml:lang="en">https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821130</mathmoddb:P1684>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820972">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">linear parameter estimation (Kiselev model)</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">nonlinear estimation of Kiselev model parameters</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P558 xml:lang="en">https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820992</mathmoddb:P558>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This task estimates the Kiselev equilibrium constant and the complex formation constant using the linearized form of the Kiselev isotherm. Experimental equilibrium coverage and concentration data are transformed and analyzed using linear regression. Although computationally simple, the approach may introduce bias due to data transformation. The estimated parameters describe adsorption affinity and the extent of complex formation among adsorbed species.</mathmoddb:P1459>
  </rdf:Description>
