  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821395">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534292"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">estimation of vertical root biomass distribution</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">quantify how root growth is distributed across soil layers</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This research problem concerns the representation of how crop root biomass is distributed vertically within the soil profile. Root distribution determines which soil layers contribute to water and nutrient uptake. A realistic description must account for functional root activity rather than only geometric depth. The problem focuses on linking root growth allocation to soil-layer-specific conditions, such as water availability. Accurate representation of vertical root distribution is essential for modeling soil-plant interactions and crop responses to environmental stress.</mathmoddb:P1459>
  </rdf:Description>
