  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821384">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">root biomass distribution equation</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">allocates root biomass growth according to water use</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This equation distributes the total daily increase in root biomass among soil layers in proportion to plant water use in each layer. The formulation assumes that layers contributing more to water uptake also receive a larger share of new root growth. Normalization by total water use ensures conservation of total root biomass increment across layers. The approach yields realistic vertical root distributions under non-limiting conditions and dynamically adjusts allocation when soil water or root stress factors reduce water uptake.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P989>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Δ&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Δ&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;T&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mfrac&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;u&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;munderover&gt;&lt;mo movablelimits="false" stretchy="false"&gt;∑&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;M&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/munderover&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;u&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mfrac&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Δ&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;T&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Δ&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;W&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;u&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775295">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534292"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">plate with a hole</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">simulating the strength of a plate with a cylindrical hole</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">A plate with a hole can refer to various things, including a structural element with a pre-formed opening, a component used for anchoring or connecting, or a surface imperfection like a void or pop-out. The specific context determines the implications of the hole and its impact on the concrete's behavior or function. (AI within a Google search)</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P1690 xml:lang="en">https://en.wikiversity.org/wiki/Elasticity/Plate_with_hole_in_tension</mathmoddb:P1690>
  </rdf:Description>
