    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">initial product 2 concentration (bi bi reaction ordered without product 2 - Michaelis Menten model)</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">initial concentration</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P558 xml:lang="en">https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6773641</mathmoddb:P558>
    <mathmoddb:P989>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;c&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;P&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mn&gt;2&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;(&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;t&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;0&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;)&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;0&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;t&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;c&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;P&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mn&gt;2&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N120d18d069684cfda999ed197b9bf232">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821221"/>
    <owl:annotatedTarget>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;A&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</owl:annotatedTarget>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/P983"/>
    <mathmoddb:P984>https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821215</mathmoddb:P984>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6684687">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534292"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">uni uni reaction with competitive partial inhibition</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">uni uni reaction with inhibition</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">Enzyme (E) and Substrate (S) form an enzyme-substrate complex (ES), which catalyzes the formation of product (P). Rates for complex formation and dissociation are k₁ and k₋₁, k₂ is the rate of the rate-determining enzymatic step of product formation. Free enzyme and the enzyme-substrate complex may bind an inhibitor (I) to form an enzyme-inhibitor (EI) and enzyme-inhibitor-substrate complex (EIS) with k₃ or k₋₃ and k₄ or k₋₄ as rates of inhibitor complex formation and depletion. Enzyme-inhibitor complex and enzyme-inhibitor-substrate convert into each other with rates k₅ and k₋₅. From the enzyme-inhibitor-substrate complex product is formed with rate k₂. Properly this is a mixed partial inhibition in which the inhibitor does not affect the turnover rate.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P1684 xml:lang="en">https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6684665</mathmoddb:P1684>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821298">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">heat unit response shape parameters</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">shape parameters of HUF sigmoid curve</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">These crop-specific parameters determine the shape and steepness of the sigmoid relationship between heat unit index and heat unit factor. They are computed by fitting the heat unit factor equation to two predefined calibration points. The parameters remain constant throughout the simulation. They reflect phenological characteristics specific to each crop.</mathmoddb:P1459>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6822035">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">total soil nitrogen supply equation</rdfs:label>
    <schema:description xml:lang="en">aggregates nitrogen supply from all soil layers</schema:description>
    <mathmoddb:P1459 xml:lang="en">This equation computes the total nitrogen supply available to the crop by summing the layer-specific nitrogen supply rates. It represents the total nitrogen that could be taken up by mass flow on a given day. The result serves as an intermediate quantity used to compare soil nitrogen availability with crop nitrogen demand. It links soil-layer processes to whole-plant nitrogen uptake.</mathmoddb:P1459>
    <mathmoddb:P989>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;S&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;munderover&gt;&lt;mo movablelimits="false" stretchy="false"&gt;∑&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo stretchy="false"&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;M&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/munderover&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P989>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;S&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
    <mathmoddb:P983>&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline"&gt;&lt;mrow data-mjx-texclass="ORD"&gt;&lt;mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"&gt;&lt;mi&gt;U&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mstyle&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;</mathmoddb:P983>
  </rdf:Description>
